On-device AI means using small, powerful computers (like your phone or smartwatch) to do smart tasks **without needing a computer or the internet**. Imagine this: when you take a photo with your phone, the AI (a special type of computer that learns from data) quickly analyzes the image and tells you what's in it, like "That's a cat." But instead of sending the photo to a server (a big computer that handles all the data), the AI does the work right on your phone. This makes it faster, safer (since it doesn’t share your data), and works even when you’re offline. 🚀

